Subject: [flux] Pack the chrome://flux resources into resources.pak

build_webui() emits flux_resources.pak, but a pak nothing repacks is a pak
nothing loads: SetupWebUIDataSource resolves IDR_FLUX_* through the
ResourceBundle, so without this chrome://flux serves an empty page at runtime
while building perfectly cleanly.

Two edits, because the pak list and the target that produces it are declared
separately: chrome_paks.gni names the file, //chrome/browser/resources:resources
pulls in the target that generates it.

--- a/chrome/browser/resources/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/BUILD.gn
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@
       "drive_picker_host:resources",
       "drive_picker_host/untrusted:resources",
       "feedback:resources",
+      "flux:resources",
       "gaia_auth_host:resources",
       "glic/experimental_opt_in:resources",
       "glic/selection_overlay:resources",
--- a/chrome/chrome_paks.gni
+++ b/chrome/chrome_paks.gni
@@ -227,6 +227,7 @@
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/drive_picker_host_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/drive_picker_host_untrusted_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/feedback_resources.pak",
+        "$root_gen_dir/chrome/flux_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/gaia_auth_host_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/glic_experimental_opt_in_resources.pak",
         "$root_gen_dir/chrome/glic_untrusted_resources.pak",
